trait-language-spessnish-name = Spessnish
trait-language-spessnish-desc =
    Spessnish finds it's roots amongst some of the first traversers to the stars, that being the fair people of the Earth country of Mexico. It features many words
    from the language known as "Spanish", but with differentiated meanings for words. It remains in popular use by descendants of those very same travelers, tourists to Earth,
    and modern natives of Mexico and Spain.

trait-language-hegemonic-name = Hegemonic
trait-language-hegemonic-desc =
    The language of the Galactic Hegemony. While NanoTrasen Officials look down upon speakers of this language, it is not technically treasonous. It features characters from the
    Latin alphabet with an unconventional yet harmonic sound and sequencing. It is mainly spoken by citizens, soldiers, and officials of the Galctic Hegemony, but sees use
    by those who find themselves aligned with the Galactic Hegemony's ideals of a unified universe.

trait-language-sovblov-name = Sovblov
trait-language-sovblov-desc =
    The language of the Soviet Remnant, an obscure faction present on planet Earth. It has a slightly intimidating demeanor
    to the words spoken in it, regardless if the intent of the words is actually menacing. It is mainly spoken by loyalists of the Soviet Remnant, historians who know of the
    context behind the Space Race, and by modern enthusiasts of ushankas.
